    "field": "Paleoceanography",
    "problem": "The causes for changes in Atlantic water mass distributions during past warm periods remain mostly elusive, as interpreting single geological proxy records is challenging because local variations may not accurately reflect large-scale circulation dynamics.",
    "method": "This paper uses a state-of-the-art Earth system model to run quasi-equilibrium simulations for two periods during the last interglacial (115 ka and 125 ka), comparing the results with paleo-proxies to explain changes in deep water properties and water mass distributions in the Atlantic Ocean.",
    "task": "The task is to use a state-of-the-art Earth system model to examine and explain the changes in Atlantic deep water circulation and water mass distributions between two periods (125 ka and 115 ka) during the last interglacial by comparing simulations with geological proxy records.",
